Constraints: $p \geq 1$ and $10 - p \geq 1$, giving $p \in \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9\}$.

**Convexity/simplicity verification:** The down path (directions $330°, 300°, 270°, 240°, 210°$) has strictly decreasing $y$-coordinates, so it cannot self-intersect. The up path (directions $150°, 120°, 90°, 60°, 30°$) has strictly increasing $y$-coordinates. The down path lies in $x \in [8, 8+p\sqrt{3}/2+6]$ while the up path lies in $x \in [-p\sqrt{3}/2-6, 0]$; these ranges are disjoint ($8 > 0$), so the paths don't cross. All interior angles are 150°, confirming convexity. Every value of $p$ yields a valid convex equiangular dodecagon.

